From b05bedf2691c0e414762aa403c6f9e1b8b8c1eab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:48:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] fix(auth): stop LDAP sync from taking over
 password-bearing local accounts; enforce TOTP per account

Since 7449b62 _sync_one_user set auth_provider='ldap' on every matched row,
including local accounts with a password that were matched only by
sAMAccountName or mail. Consequences: the directory identity inherited the
row's roles at the next login (auth.py matches ldap rows by external_id), and
because login_local enforced TOTP only for auth_provider == 'local', the flip
switched off the administrator's second factor.

ldap_sync:
- _local_row_may_link(): a local row is linked only when matched by its stable
  directory identity (GUID/DN), or when it has no password, or when the
  operator opts in via LDAP_LINK_LOCAL_PASSWORD_ACCOUNTS=true. Full
  Administrator rows are never linked. Refused rows are left untouched (no
  restore, no profile rewrite, no external_id) and reported in conflicts with
  reason=local_password_account; a new local_password_skipped counter is
  returned. Like foreign-provider skips this does not suppress pruning (the
  refused row is 'local', so prune never considers it).

auth:
- TOTP is now enforced whenever user.totp_enabled is set, for the password
  path and after a successful LDAP bind (_two_factor_challenge helper).

scripts/audit-ldap-relinks.py lists rows already flipped last week
(auth_provider='ldap' AND hashed_password IS NOT NULL) and can revert chosen
ids to 'local' without touching passwords, roles or TOTP.

Tests: tests/test_ldap_sync_link_policy.py (refuse by username/email, opt-in
link, Full Admin never linked, passwordless + DN-matched rows still link) and
tests/test_login_totp_provider_independent.py (fails on the previous auth.py
for provider='ldap').

